<title>USA: Motorola introduces CDMA micro station.</title>
<headline>Motorola introduces CDMA micro station.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Thursday it introduced a suitcase-sized CDMA (code divisional multiple access) microcell base station to help wireless phone operators enhance networks.</p>
<p>The SC 601 station was designed to provide fill-in coverage where space and traffic would make station installation difficult. Areas include shopping malls, parking garages and large office buildings, Motorola said.</p>
<p>Motorola said it will begin shipping the SC 601 in December.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
